  "slug": "metabolomic-extract-96e7",
  "summary": "Public transcriptomic cohorts and single-cell deconvolution now routinely yield multi-gene prognostic and immune-associated signatures across cancer types.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational derivation of prognostic or diagnostic gene signatures from public transcriptomic cohorts and multi-omic data, usually checked across independent cohorts, with several items adding cell-state deconvolution or mechanistic follow-up. Most items rely on limma, WGCNA and LASSO-based pipelines to build risk scores, as in the colorectal eight-gene model and the lysosomal cell death lung adenocarcinoma model, whose AUCs range from 0.545 to 0.692. New elements include Statescope deconvolution resolving cancer-associated fibroblast states in 74 early-onset PDAC patients, a senescence signature that couples H&E deep-learning features with bulk, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics to predict immunotherapy response, and a multi-layer graph convolutional network integrating scRNA-derived tumor microenvironment deconvolution with multi-omics in pancreatic cancer. Mechanistic items, such as circFOXK2 driving MLL1-mediated H3K4 methylation, address function rather than patient stratification.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
